Applied by tools/build-toolchain.sh when the binutils pin is on branch
amiga-2.46, together with the two diffs beside it.

Against bebbo's binutils-gdb, branch amiga-2.46, commit
a50544a917284847c99e97d41c69ece9d5cb2fef (https://franke.ms/git/bebbo/binutils-gdb).
Backport of 6fa839d070065be84b48fb48112b42c408f4fc6b from the same branch;
drop this file when the pin reaches it.

WHAT IT FIXES

`ar` dies with SIGFPE writing the archive index of any object that has a
weak one-only section (every C++ COMDAT):

  bfd_hash_lookup <- _bfd_generic_section_already_linked
    <- amiga_slurp_symbol_table <- _bfd_compute_and_write_armap

amiga_slurp_symbol_table calls bfd_section_already_linked() to keep the
first copy of such a section.  That table is initialised only by ld; under
ar and objcopy its size is 0 and the hash modulus divides by zero.  The
toolchain build stops at libsupc++.  lto-archive-symbol-index.diff is what
makes `ar` write an index at all on this target, so it is what exposes the
crash.  The dedup now runs only when ld has set the link info.

diff --git a/bfd/amigaos.c b/bfd/amigaos.c
index 32285d5f..1ae240e3 100644
--- a/bfd/amigaos.c
+++ b/bfd/amigaos.c
@@ -3648,7 +3648,7 @@ amiga_slurp_symbol_table (bfd *abfd)
 	  section->symbol->name = section->name;
 	/* Early LTO debug sections contain a weak compilation-unit marker,
 	   but each section still has distinct contents that must be kept.  */
-	if (i && all_weak && (section->flags & SEC_DEBUGGING) == 0)
+	if (plink_info && i && all_weak && (section->flags & SEC_DEBUGGING) == 0)
 	  {
 	    /* SBF: mark the section optional */
 	    section->flags |= SEC_LINK_ONCE | SEC_LINK_DUPLICATES_DISCARD | SEC_LINK_DUPLICATES_SAME_CONTENTS;
